# Trivy vulnerability suppressions.
# Each entry MUST document why the advisory does not apply and be re-checked
# whenever dependencies change. Trivy reads this file from the repo root, so it
# is honored by both the CI scans (docker-publish, cve-trivy-scan) and local runs.

# Every entry carries an exp: date so it lapses and must be re-reviewed instead
# of silently hiding a future advisory.

# GO-2026-5932 — golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained and unsafe by design.
# x/crypto v0.58.0 comes with minio-go (S3 store, GLD-020), which links only
# golang.org/x/crypto/argon2 and blake2b (`go list -deps ./cmd/goeland-server`);
# openpgp is not in the binary and govulncheck finds no call. The only fix is an
# untagged commit: re-check when x/crypto tags a release (2026-11-25).
GO-2026-5932 exp:2027-02-25
